rikes we're going to have a health  system under strain we're going to have  a recession we're going to have tension  with the bank of England and we have the  political instability that we've seen  already so those are big big issues  which will be worsened by the fact that  we have to reassure the markets that  Britain is committed to fiscal  responsibility politically as well a  series of extremely difficult decisions  now have to be taken we are going to  have to see a combination of tax Rises  and spending cuts which will exacerbate  all of the issues that I've just  described so he has to walk this very  narrow and difficult tightrope between  satisfying investors in Britain and  satisfying his voters  because Mr sunac has to run a party  which has proved itself almost  ungovernable because  the party is deeply unpopular and likely  to become more so as the decisions he is  about to make bite you could imagine yet  another round of infighting and at that  point the calls for a general election  even if constitutionally one is not  needed will become ever more difficult  to resist there is a question of moral  and Democratic legitimacy which is  already in the air another leadership  contest would make that almost  impossible to resist  thanks for watching to read more of our  coverage on British politics click the  link and don't forget to subscribe  foreign  [Music]

